  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kuapa Kids Camps Child Labour Project (Ghana)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The health system in Sierra Leone is still recovering from the effects of the civil war.  Free health care for pregnant women and children under five years was introduced in 2010.  However the strategy for community-based approaches for maternal and child health is not being implemented.  Maternal and child death rates are still above the 2015 MDG target, and are even worse in Kambia district. This project will pilot Community Health Education in three communities in Kambia district. People will know more about basic health messages, and the importance of timely health care. The project will measure whether the model increases the number of pregnant women and children using free primary health care services. Learning from this pilot project will be used to inform the scale up of a community health education programme across the district.</narrative>
  </description>
